"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nReading Jeong You-jeong's works is suffocating.  \nThe depiction of the characters' situations and their emotions is so vivid that it's difficult to read.  \nThe terrible mistake of one night by a character named  becomes the seed of all tragedy.  \n\nIt seems that characters with psychopathic tendencies appear every time in the author's works.  \nIn this work as well, that character is indeed quite tenacious.  \n\nThis work seems to be a story about two tragic versions of fatherly love.\nA tragic fatherly love that plunged his son into hell through a momentary mistake but tries to save him by sacrificing himself at the last moment.  \nThe other is a twisted and destructive fatherly love that regards his daughter as a possession and uses his dead daughter as a tool for his own revenge.\nThe stark contrast between these two fathers seems to throw a heavy question:   "